Optimal Loading Progress

Current state
- The reload-flow root cause is now addressed in code.
- Save-slot selection no longer starts a live gameplay location load before the loading overlay is up.
- Save loads now run under `LoadGameFlow` so `Start Game` and `Load Game` can be tracked separately.
- Reveal release now waits for pending deferred location activation work, so environment/UI/light activation is supposed to stay behind black.
- Gameplay scene lights are restored before `alphaOut` starts, with the delayed cleanup path kept only as fallback.
- Same-location gameplay reloads under an active overlay now rebuild the location instead of skipping as a duplicate pending load.
- Loading progress UI now emits a one-shot warning if the percent/text carrier still is not armed on the frame after `BeginLoadingProgressUiAfterFadeIn()`.

Root cause fixed in this pass
- `LoadMenuInput` was triggering `LocationManager.UpdateLocation(...)` and `RequestLocationLoad(...)` before `startGame`, which allowed the gameplay location to begin loading before the overlay.
- `SingleSceneManager` was also resolving the save location through `LocationManager.UpdateLocation(...)` before the gameplay-under-black phase, which split ownership of gameplay activation.
- The gameplay load path could dispatch both `LocationUpdated` and `RequestLocationLoad` for the same change, creating inconsistent reload timing.
- Reveal gating treated blocking location activation as a blocker, but not deferred location activation work, so fade-out could begin while late environment/UI/light work was still pending.
- Scene lights were restored too late, which let the player model appear black for visible frames after reveal started.

What changed
- Gameplay load flow is now the only owner of save-load location activation.
- Save locations are staged and consumed exactly once from `ApplyGameplayStateUnderBlack()`.
- Changed-location gameplay requests now go through `LocationUpdated` once; same-location refreshes go through `RequestLocationLoad` once.
- `WaitForStreamingIdleBeforeUnlock()` and `WaitForRevealActivationSettle()` now both block on `LocationManager.HasPendingDeferredActivationWork`.
- Reveal logging now treats deferred location activation as a first-class blocker.
- Save-load overlay telemetry now reports `LoadGameFlow`.

